@startuml
title Strijder power entry and backup path - conceptual connectivity
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Vehicle source\nNominal 12 V class; envelope TBD" as BAT
rectangle "F100\nSource-adjacent harness fuse" as F100
rectangle "J101 / F101\nPower inlet / coordinated service fuse" as J101
rectangle "D101\nCoordinated surge suppressor" as D101
rectangle "U101 + Q101/Q102\nReverse / overvoltage protection\nBack-to-back FET reference circuit TBD" as PROT
rectangle "L101 / C101 / C102\nDamped input filter" as FILTER
rectangle "U102\nChemistry-specific charger\nInput budget / temperature inhibit" as CHG
rectangle "BAT101 / BMS / F102\nQualified backup pack\nSource-adjacent pack fuse" as PACK
rectangle "U103\nSource priority / reverse isolation\nVehicle preferred; discharge path" as MUX
rectangle "U104\nRail conversion bank\nBuck / buck-boost as required" as DC
rectangle "Protected peripheral branches\nSee peripheral-branch.puml" as BR
rectangle "U105\nAlways-on supervisor\nShutdown / charging / load shedding" as MCU
rectangle "PWR_RTN\nDedicated power return" as RTN

BAT --> F100 : positive
F100 --> J101 : VBAT_RAW
J101 --> PROT : VBAT_FUSED
J101 --> D101 : VBAT_FUSED shunt tap
D101 --> RTN : transient return
PROT --> FILTER : VBAT_PROT
FILTER --> MUX : VBAT_FILTERED / source A
FILTER --> CHG : VBAT_FILTERED
CHG --> PACK : controlled charge path
PACK --> MUX : PACK_OUT / source B
MUX --> DC : VSYS_BACKED
DC --> BR : VPERIPH_n
MUX --> MCU : dedicated always-on regulator
MCU ..> CHG : CHARGE_EN / current budget
MCU ..> BR : EN_n / shutdown
BAT -- RTN : negative return
PACK -- RTN : pack return
DC -- RTN : power return
BR -- RTN : sized branch returns

note right of PROT
  Example family: LM7480-Q1; not selected.
  Controller pins, MOSFET orientation, gate
  components and suppression require ECAD.
end note
note right of MUX
  VSYS_BACKED is NOT a fixed 12 V rail.
  Charging and discharge paths must not
  create cross-source or circulating current.
end note
note bottom of RTN
  Filter capacitor, charger and supervisor returns also connect
  to PWR_RTN; physical current loops require layout design.
  Chassis/shields are not assumed power-return conductors.
  Warning lamps use separate assessed fused distribution.
  Signal arrows are control intent, not controller pin numbers.
end note
legend bottom
  CONCEPTUAL / NOT FOR FABRICATION
  Fuse values, voltage limits, pack, ratings and all pin numbers TBD.
endlegend
@enduml
